# Path prefixes that harness/check-conventions.sh skips (playbook docs/16 s6.2). This file belongs
# to this repository; the playbook installer does not write or refresh it.
#
# What docs/ko/ is: this repository's Korean control documents. They are the project's own original
# writing, NOT a reproduced external corpus, and the Korean and English sides are peers with neither
# authoritative over the other (UPDATES.md section 2.2, and the copyright boundary in CLAUDE.md).
# docs/16 s6.2 reserves this file for reproduced external corpora, so this entry is a recorded
# exception to that rule, not an instance of it.
#
# Why it is listed: the documents keep the Korean renderings of IT terms that their readers use
# (log, backup, network, data, service), and the term rule [2] of the playbook v0.10.11 checker,
# which no longer exempts Korean documents, reports them 1,598 times in 90 of the 94 files
# (2026-10-24). The upgrade to v0.10.11 left the corpus text unchanged. Rewriting those renderings
# into English would also change the Korean control titles in extended/catalog/controls.json and
# so the names extended/manifest.json publishes, which makes removing this entry an owner decision.
#
# What it costs: the checker skips these files for every check, including [1] forbidden unicode.
# tools/check_corpus.py check [13] scans every control document for the eight forbidden characters
# of docs/16 s2.1 instead, and the corpus-integrity check in CI runs it.
#
# docs/en/ is deliberately NOT listed: it is clean on every check, so excluding it would waive
# nothing and only widen the carve-out. docs/ko/ alone stays under the 40% limit of check [0], so
# this repository declares no harness/corpus-repo either.
docs/ko/
